    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d220">

                <pb facs="0311" n="300" sameAs="frus:frus1937v02/pg300"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.114 St. Pierre-Miquelon/460: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bullitt</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-02-13T18:00:00+00:00">February 13, 1937—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 13—2:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>206. In supplement to my 204, February 13, 2 p.m. I saw Blum<anchor n="37"
                        xml:id="d220-f1"/> this afternoon and expressed our views amicably but
                    vigorously. He promised to look into the question personally at once.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bullitt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d220-f1" n="37" xml:id="d220-f1-content">
                <p>Léon Blum, President of the French Council of Ministers.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
